        "text": "Thanks all for the thoughts, they sorted out something I had been going back and forth on. I _immensely_ appreciated the detailed feedback <@U01DZUA88S1>. You'll notice I largely tried to follow it while setting things up.\n\nOn the package pages we now have two cite buttons as.\n\n1. One for the package, which just gives you citation() and suggests the authors' inst\/CITATION where there is one. \n2. One for the numbers on the page, which names the dated data release the values came from, so a citation still resolves later even though the page itself updates daily. \nAnd we now have a Zenodo DOI now as well: 10.5281\/zenodo.21843040. So, probably there's less of a rush or need now for a paper I suppose.\n\nGuidance and worked examples are at <https:\/\/r-observatory.thecoatlessprofessor.com\/about\/cite|r-observatory.thecoatlessprofessor.com\/about\/cite>\n\n<@U055CT9LSR5>, your ggmice page has both buttons on it whenever you need them.",
